{
  "comment": "Why: the frost sectors are cold and empty, so the table has fewer rolls (roll bonus minus one: the cold keeps things asleep) and bigger fights when they do come (budget scale 1.1). Its flavour is range (strays shooting down a long hall), packs (wolves, direwolves), bears, and the wind (breezes) that comes to warmth.",
  "description": "Packed ice, snow, spruce and calcite: archers of the cold, wolves and bears, and the dead that never thawed. Sparse and quiet; the fights are long and come in bursts.",
  "rollBonus": -1,
  "budgetScale": 1.1,
  "defaultFaction": "undead",
  "entries": [
